              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "On paper the Weimar Republic was strikingly modern: it gave the vote to all adults — including women for the first time — and guaranteed broad civil rights. Yet within fourteen years it was dead. The exam's chapter on this era is called *Geschichte und Verantwortung* (history and responsibility), and it wants you to grasp *why* a real democracy failed — because that failure is the reason today's Germany is built the way it is."
