              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Then came economic catastrophe — twice. In **1923** hyperinflation made money almost worthless; savings evaporated overnight. The economy briefly stabilised, but the worldwide **Great Depression** that began in **1929** threw millions out of work. Desperate, frightened voters abandoned the moderate parties and turned to the radicals promising order and revenge. The Nazi party (the **NSDAP**) grew from a fringe group into the largest party in parliament."
