              "text": "The system also had design flaws that its enemies exploited. Article 48 of the Weimar constitution let the directly elected **Reichspräsident** (Reich President) rule by emergency decree, bypassing parliament. Strict proportional representation produced many small parties and unstable, short-lived coalitions. By the early 1930s Germany was increasingly governed by emergency decree rather than by parliamentary majorities. The democratic constitution's own tools were being turned against democracy itself."
