              "text": "The wartime alliance did not survive the peace. The three Western powers wanted a democratic, market-based Germany; the Soviet Union wanted a communist one in its own image. As mistrust hardened into a global stand-off between West and East — the **Kalter Krieg** (*Cold War*) — the two halves of Germany drifted apart. An early flashpoint came in 1948–49, when the Soviet Union blockaded all land routes into West Berlin and the Western allies kept the city alive for nearly a year by flying in food and coal — the **Luftbrücke** (*Berlin Airlift*). By 1949 the split was formal: two German states, born the same year, facing each other across the front line of the Cold War."
