              "text": "Reunification could have happened in two very different constitutional ways, and the choice between them shaped modern Germany. **Article 146** of the **Grundgesetz** (Basic Law) imagined the whole German people, once united, giving itself a brand-new constitution. **Article 23** — in the wording it had at the time — allowed *other German territories* simply to accede to the existing Federal Republic and adopt the Basic Law as it already stood."
